1. Why is Random Forest considered an Ensemble Learning algorithm?
Random Forest combines multiple Decision Tree to make a single, stronger application.
Each tree votes or averages its output, and the final result is based on the collective decision-
that's why its an ensemble(a group of models working together).

2. Is Random Forest an example of Bagging or Boosting?
It is an example of Bagging (Bootstrap Aggregating).
It trains many Decision Trees independtly (parallel) on different random subsets of data and features,
then aggregates their predictions.
